$ 100 Welcome to help
Welcome to on-line help! On-line help makes your job much easier because
you don't have to constantly refer to a manual or a .DOC file.

You can call on help at most times by pressing the F1 key.

Help is context-sensitive: it will display the most useful information
depending on the job you are doing. For example, pressing F1 while
on the Condition screen will go directly to help for that screen.

On-line help contains hyperlinks: a link that takes you to another part of
help. Hyperlinks are displayed in yellow.
To move the cursor, use the arrow keys, HOME and END. TAB highlights the
next hyperlink, and RETURN activates the current hyperlink.

Try it now: either use the arrows or TAB to activate this hyperlink:
 <1000, Help Contents >
$ 105 Reactions and the Data column
There are at present these possible reactions:

Go to screen         ³ Loads another room. Data (opt): Which side of room
                     ³  man appears on (1000=left, 2000=right, 3000=bottom,
                     ³  4000=top). Can add offset of position.
No action            ³ Ignores the event.
Blocked: Can't walk  ³ The man can't move.
Man dies             ³ The man dies.
Run animation        ³ Runs an animation. Hit F10 to edit it.
Display message      ³ Displays a message (0-100 room, 500-990 global).
Remove object        ³ The object disappears.
Remove obj, add inv  ³ Remove the object and add inventory number Data.
Add inventory        ³ Adds the specified item to the player's inventory.
Run script           ³ Runs a block from the text script file.
Run graphical script ³ Use graphical script for response, hit F10 to edit.
Play sound           ³ Plays sound effect SOUND%d.WAV or SOUND%d.VOC
Play FLI/FLC         ³ Plays FLIC%d.FLC or FLIC%d.FLI animation file.
Turn object on       ³ Turns on an object removed with "Remove object".

See the AC.DOC file for a more detailed description.
$ 999 Error
